Q1 – AI Mental Model (MCQ)
What is the most accurate description of how tools like ChatGPT or Copilot work?
A. They search the internet for correct answers
B. They predict likely responses based on patterns in data 
C. They reason like humans
D. They always return factual information

right answer: They predict likely responses based on patterns in data

Q2 – AI Strengths (MCQ)
Which task is AI generally BEST suited for?
A. Making final business decisions
B. Generating perfect, error-free content
C. Drafting and summarizing information quickly 
D. Replacing human judgment entirely

right answer: Drafting and summarizing information quickly


Q3 – AI Limitations (MCQ)
Which statement about AI output is TRUE?
A. AI outputs are always accurate
B. AI understands the meaning of what it writes
C. AI may produce confident but incorrect information 
D. AI remembers past conversations across tools

right answer: AI may produce confident but incorrect information

Q4 – Prompting Fundamentals (MCQ)
Which prompt is MOST effective?
A. “Summarize”
B. “Summarize this”
C. “Summarize this meeting and extract 5 action items for the leadership team” 
D. “Tell me what happened”

right answer: “Summarize this meeting and extract 5 action items for the leadership team”

Q5 – Prompt Iteration (MCQ)
If the AI output isn’t what you want, what should you do first?
A. Stop using AI
B. Ask the same prompt again
C. Refine the instructions or add context 
D. Assume the tool is broken

right answer: Refine the instructions or add context

Q6 – Applied Scenario (Judgment)
You need to prepare a client update quickly. What is the BEST use of AI?
A. Ask AI to send the email directly to the client
B. Ask AI to draft the email, then review and edit it yourself 
C. Copy the AI output without reading it
D. Avoid using AI for client communication

right answer: Ask AI to draft the email, then review and edit it yourself

Q7 – Applied Scenario (Judgment)
AI gives you an answer that “looks right” but feels off. What should you do?
A. Trust it anyway
B. Ignore the feeling
C. Verify key facts or cross-check with another source 
D. Assume AI is wrong and delete everything

right answer: Verify key facts or cross-check with another source

Q8 – Safety & Quality (MCQ)
Which information should generally NOT be entered into public AI tools?
A. Public marketing copy
B. Generic meeting notes
C. Customer personal data or confidential information 
D. Brainstorming ideas

right answer: Customer personal data or confidential information

Q9 – Confidence Self-Assessment
How confident do you feel using AI tools in your daily work?
1. Not confident
2. Slightly confident
3. Moderately confident
4. Confident
5. Very confident
(No right/wrong answer)


Q10 – Usage Frequency
How often do you currently use AI tools at work?
A. Never
B. Occasionally (once a month or less)
